# Canvas Update on Every Ship

Whenever you **ship a code change, bug fix, UX update, or doc reconciliation that affects field/dispatcher behavior**, update the relevant canvas **before** telling the user the work is done.

## Which canvas

| Change type | Canvas file |
|-------------|-------------|
| Bug / #issues-found / KI-* fix | `canvases/issues-found-fix-tracker.canvas.tsx` |
| Phase ship, feature, build stamp | `canvases/current-state.canvas.tsx` |
| Icebox / roadmap idea | `canvases/idea-vault.canvas.tsx` |

Canvas path: `C:\Users\daday\.cursor\projects\c-Projects-PROJECT-DISPATCHER-TOOL\canvases\`

## Mandatory on every update

1. **Status** — set item to `in_progress` when starting, `completed` when shipped (or add a new row if none exists).
2. **Ship metadata** — `VC_BUILD` stamp, script `?v=` bump, commit hash if known.
3. **User test steps** — numbered steps the user can run on device to confirm the fix worked. Not agent-only Playwright notes.

## User test steps format (required)

Each shipped item must include **`userTestSteps`** — an array of short, ordered strings:

```
1. Force-reload PWA until BUILD shows <stamp> (VC DEBUG overlay)
2. Log in as <tech>
3. Do X — expect Y
4. ...
```

Cover: **how to open the app fresh**, **where to tap**, **what should happen**, **what failure looks like**.

For UI changes, note Playwright may have already verified — user steps are still required.

## Done checklist (add to fix-tracker flow)

```
[ ] Canvas updated — status + userTestSteps
[ ] Code committed + pushed (when user asks or session ships)
[ ] Deployed if field app (firebase deploy --only hosting)
[ ] Tell user which canvas to open and which # to test
```

**Do not report "done" without updating the canvas.** The user uses canvases to track progress and to know how to verify on device.

## Pair with fix-tracker rule

Fix tracker items also need file, line, before, after, root cause, model — see `canvas-fix-tracker-handoff.mdc`. **`userTestSteps` is additive and mandatory for every shipped item.**
